! ---- Ray failure diagnostics: the message catalog (src/ray-messages.f90) ----
! The legacy tracer prints, while the MSG flag is on, a line
!     " RAY FAILURE OCCURRED AT SURFACE n"
! followed by a reason for every ray it cannot trace.  The global-free engine is
! pure and cannot print: it records which message legacy would have printed (an
! id of mod_ray_messages) and the router prints the recorded messages with the
! same routines legacy uses.  This fixture runs the failing rays with the engine
! ON (the default) and its .ref is identical, apart from the RAYENGINE lines, to
! the output with RAYENGINE OFF.  Output the legacy tracer sends to unit 6
! (PRINT *) is not captured by the test runner and so is not in the .ref.
!
! Which commands reach the engine.  Every case below is followed by a
! RAYENGINE report whose "engine" count is the number of rays the engine took
! and whose "declined" counts show nothing went to the legacy tracer.
!   Part 1  GET <operand> traces its rays with RAY semantics and MSG on.
!   Part 2  the RAY command (and so RSI, which sends RAY) also asks for plot-ray
!           capture (GRASET); the router reproduces that capture (GLVERT/GLPRY)
!           on the engine's ray.  These are the only commands that exercise
!           CAOB (clear aperture / obscuration checking) and wavelength 0.
!
! Messages (id in mod_ray_messages, legacy routine, text):
!   MSG_TIR              INTERACK  TOTAL INTERNAL REFLECTION (at the failing surface)
!   MSG_AIM_NOT_CONVERGED  RAYTRA  RAY FAILED TO CONVERGE TO REFERENCE SURFACE
!                                  RAY-AIM POINT (surface = reference surface)
!   MSG_ZERO_WAVELENGTH    RAYTRA  RAY CAN NOT BE TRACED AT ZERO WAVELENGTH
!   MSG_CLAP_*           CACHEK    RAY BLOCKED BY <shape> CLEAR APERTURE
!   MSG_COBS_*           CACHEK    RAY BLOCKED BY <shape> OBSCURATION
! Not reachable from a command: MSG_TIR_NOT_MET (TIRTESTER = sin(i)*+-1 can
! never exceed 1), MSG_NO_AIM_SOLUTION (all four aiming derivatives exactly zero;
! ENGINETEST checks the id on its failure branch), IPOLY shapes (their vertex
! file cannot be provided to a script; ENGINETEST checks them synthetically),
! and negative clear aperture types (no setter stores one).
! (Legacy also had two ungated debug outputs on these paths and could leave
! MSG off after a multiple-aperture surface; those were removed from the legacy
! tracer -- see src/ray-messages.f90 -- so both tracers print the same.)
RAYENGINE ON

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Part 1: engine-routed failing rays
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

! case 1.1: a ray that traces: nothing is printed
RES osdtriplet
FOB 0
RAYENGINE RESET
GET PACM
RAYENGINE

! case 1.2: with a 100 unit entrance pupil the marginal rays fail to refract.
! Expected: " RAY FAILURE OCCURRED AT SURFACE 2", "TOTAL INTERNAL REFLECTION"
RES osdtriplet
EPD 100
FOB 0
RAYENGINE RESET
GET PACM
GET SACM
RAYENGINE

! case 1.3: ray aiming with at most one aim iteration cannot converge.
! Expected: " RAY FAILURE OCCURRED AT SURFACE 3" (the reference surface),
! "RAY FAILED TO CONVERGE TO REFERENCE SURFACE RAY-AIM POINT"
RES osdtriplet
RAYAIM ON
FOB 0.7
NRAITR 1
RAYENGINE RESET
GET PACM
GET SACM
RAYENGINE
NRAITR 100

! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Part 2: the RAY command (plot-ray capture, see above)
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

! case 2.1: TIR.  Expected: surface 2, TOTAL INTERNAL REFLECTION, once for each
! of the first four rays; the fifth traces
RES osdtriplet
FOB 0
RAYENGINE RESET
RAY 0 20
RAY 0 -20
RAY 20 0
RAY 20 20
RAY 0 0.5
RAYENGINE

! case 2.2: aim not converging.  Expected: surface 3, RAY FAILED TO CONVERGE ...
! for the first three rays; the fourth, with an explicit fifth number, is traced
! with MSG off and prints nothing
RES osdtriplet
RAYAIM ON
FOB 0
NRAITR 1
RAY 0 0.5
RAY 0 0.5 2
RAY CAOB 0 0.5
RAY 0 0.5 1 1 1
NRAITR 100

! case 2.3: wavelength 6 has no wavelength.  Expected: surface 0, RAY CAN NOT BE
! TRACED AT ZERO WAVELENGTH (only for wavelength 6, 7); wavelength 1 traces
RES osdtriplet
FOB 0
RAY 0 0.5 6
RAY 0 0.5 7
RAY 0 0.5 1

! case 2.4: blocked by a clear aperture, one shape per case, 0.5 across at
! surface 2 (the ray at relative pupil 0.9 is 4.08 high there).  CAOB turns the
! aperture check on; a RAY without it is not blocked.
! Expected: surface 2, RAY BLOCKED BY CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE for the first and
! third ray (the one at 0.1 passes, the one without CAOB is not checked)
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP 0.5
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0 0.1
RAY CAOB 0.9 0
RAY 0 0.9

! Expected: surface 2, RAY BLOCKED BY RECTANGULAR CLEAR APERTURE, first two rays
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP RECT 0.5 0.5
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.9 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.1

! Expected: surface 2, RAY BLOCKED BY ELLIPTICAL CLEAR APERTURE, all three rays
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP ELIP 0.5 0.4
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.9 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.1

! Expected: surface 2, RAY BLOCKED BY RACETRACK CLEAR APERTURE, first two rays
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP RCTK 0.5 0.5 0 0 0.2
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.9 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.1

! Expected: surface 2, RAY BLOCKED BY POLYGON CLEAR APERTURE, all three rays
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP POLY 0.5 5
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.9 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.1

! case 2.5: blocked by an obscuration at surface 3 (the rays at 0.2 and at 0.1
! across hit it; the one at 0.9 passes).
! Expected: surface 3, RAY BLOCKED BY CIRCULAR OBSCURATION, for the first and
! third ray
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
COBS 3
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.2
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.1 0

! Expected: surface 3, RAY BLOCKED BY RECTANGULAR OBSCURATION, first and third ray
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
COBS RECT 3 3
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.2
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.1 0

! Expected: surface 3, RAY BLOCKED BY ELLIPTICAL OBSCURATION, first and third ray
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
COBS ELIP 3 3
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.2
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.1 0

! Expected: surface 3, RAY BLOCKED BY RACETRACK OBSCURATION, first and third ray
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
COBS RCTK 3 3 0 0 1
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.2
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.1 0

! Expected: surface 3, RAY BLOCKED BY POLYGON OBSCURATION, first and third ray
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
COBS POLY 3 6
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.2
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.1 0

! case 2.6: erase regions and a footblock cancel or skip the check.
! Expected: three messages for the four rays, in order: surface 2 CIRCULAR CLEAR
! APERTURE, surface 4 CIRCULAR OBSCURATION, surface 2 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP 0.5
CLAP ERASE 3 0 0
CHG 4
COBS 3
COBS ERASE 1 0 0
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0 0.1
RAY CAOB 0 0.5
RAY CAOB 0.7 0.7

! Expected: two messages, both surface 4 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE (surface 2 is
! footblocked, so its aperture is never checked)
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP 0.5
FOOTBLOK YES
CHG 4
CLAP 0.9
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0 0.1
RAY CAOB 0 0.5

! case 2.7: several apertures on one surface (MULTCLAP, MULTCOBS).  Only the
! last clear-aperture entry reports, so a ray every entry blocks prints once.
! Expected: surface 5 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE for the first and third ray (they
! pass surface 2 through an entry before the last and are blocked at surface 5;
! legacy used to leave MSG off after such a pass and so printed nothing for
! them), surface 2 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE for the second and fourth.
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP 1
MULTCLAP 1 0 10 0
MULTCLAP 2 0 3 0
MULTCLAP 3 3 0 0
MULTCLAP 4 0 -10 0
CHG 5
CLAP 0.3
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.5
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.5 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.2

! ... the same with an obscuration on surface 2.  Expected, one message per ray,
! in order: surface 5 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE; surface 2 CIRCULAR CLEAR
! APERTURE; surface 2 CIRCULAR OBSCURATION (a ray blocked by the MULTCOBS
! entry); surface 2 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 2
CLAP 1
COBS 0.2
MULTCLAP 1 0 10 0
MULTCLAP 2 0 3 0
MULTCLAP 3 3 0 0
MULTCLAP 4 0 -10 0
MULTCOBS 1 0 2.27 0
CHG 5
CLAP 0.3
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.5
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.5 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.2

! ... MULTCOBS entries alone.  Expected: surface 3 CIRCULAR OBSCURATION for the
! first two rays
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 3
COBS 0.5
MULTCOBS 1 0 8 0
MULTCOBS 2 0 3.52 0
MULTCOBS 3 3.52 0 0
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0.9 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.0
RAY CAOB 0 0.5

! case 2.8: apertures on several surfaces at once, a ray blocked by the first
! one it meets.  Expected, in order: surface 1 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE, surface 2
! RECTANGULAR CLEAR APERTURE, surface 1 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE, surface 4
! ELLIPTICAL OBSCURATION, surface 1 CIRCULAR CLEAR APERTURE; the last ray has no
! CAOB and is not checked
RES osdtriplet
U L
CHG 1
CLAP 2
CHG 2
CLAP RECT 1 1
CHG 4
COBS ELIP 0.5 0.5
CHG 5
CLAP RCTK 1 1 0 0 0.3
EOS
FOB 0
RAY CAOB 0 0.9
RAY CAOB 0 0.4
RAY CAOB 0.3 0.3
RAY CAOB 0 0.0
RAY CAOB 0 1.0
RAY 0 0.9
